' Library Management Application — Business Workflow Diagram
' Auto-split from library-management-business-workflow.puml
' Render this file individually to avoid HTTP header size limits

@startuml Recommendation_Generation_Workflow
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #F5F5F5
skinparam titleFontSize 16

title Recommendation Generation Workflow\n(FR-007, FR-008, FR-009, FR-010)

start

:Receive Version Comparison Result\nper library;

if (New version released?) then (yes)

  |Upgrade Assessment (FR-007)|
  :Evaluate whether organization\ncan upgrade to new version;
  if (Upgrade feasible?) then (yes)
    :Recommendation: **Upgrade Available**;
  else (no)
    :Recommendation: **Existing Version Sufficient**;
  endif

  |Pros/Cons — Upgrade Path (FR-008)|
  partition "Generate Pros for Upgrading" {
    :Analyze release notes for\nnew features and fixes;
    :Identify benefits of moving\nto latest version;
    :List upgrade pros;
  }
  partition "Generate Cons for Upgrading" {
    :Identify risks of upgrading\n(e.g., breaking changes);
    :Consider compatibility with\nexisting applications;
    :List upgrade cons;
  }

  |Pros/Cons — No-Upgrade Path (FR-009)|
  partition "Generate Pros for Not Upgrading" {
    :Identify stability benefits\nof current version;
    :Note known working state\nin existing applications;
    :List no-upgrade pros;
  }
  partition "Generate Cons for Not Upgrading" {
    :Identify risks of staying\non current version;
    :Note missing fixes/features\nin new release;
    :List no-upgrade cons;
  }

else (no)

  |Current Version Guidance|
  :Recommendation: **Existing Version is Current**;
  :No upgrade action required\nat this time;
  :Include current version\nstatus in output;

endif

|Recommendation Content (FR-010)|
:Compile recommendation report per library:\n• Library Name\n• DB Version vs Latest Version\n• Upgrade decision guidance\n• Pros and Cons (if applicable)\n• Release Notes summary;

:Pass recommendation content\nto Notification Service;

stop

note right
  **Business Rule**
  Every new version release must produce:
  1. Can I upgrade? OR Existing is enough?
  2. Pros and cons if upgraded
  3. Pros and cons if not upgraded
end note

@enduml
